.TH KLVTOOL-DECODE 1 "1970-01-01" "klvtool dev" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
klvtool\-decode \- Decode MISB ST 0601 KLV records from an MPEG\-TS file.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
klvtool decode \-\-input <file.ts> [\-\-format ndjson|text|csv] [\-\-pid N] [\-\-out <path>] [\-\-strict] [\-\-raw] [\-\-step] [\-\-view auto|pretty|raw] [\-\-schema <urn>]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Decode MISB ST 0601 KLV metadata from an MPEG\-TS file into typed records.
.PP
Use this after `klvtool inspect` to validate a likely metadata PID or to review packets in a terminal\-friendly view. The \-\-raw flag includes raw bytes per item: hex (0x...) in text and csv formats, base64 in NDJSON. The \-\-step flag enables one\-handed packet navigation in pretty text view: r=next, w=previous, d=next diagnostic, e=next error, q=quit.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI(default ndjson)\fR
output format: ndjson, text, or csv
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR
MPEG\-TS input path
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR
write output to a file instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-pid\fR
limit decoding to a specific KLV stream PID (0 = all)
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
include raw bytes per item (hex in text/csv, base64 in NDJSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-schema\fR
override auto\-detection with a specific spec URN
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR
step through decoded packets interactively
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
exit non\-zero if any error\-severity diagnostic is emitted
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI(default auto)\fR
presentation mode: auto, pretty, or raw
.SH "OUTPUT FORMAT"
NDJSON, one JSON object per decoded KLV packet (default \-\-format=ndjson). The \-\-format=text and \-\-format=csv variants are for human review and are not contractual.
.SS Fields
.TP
\fBschema\fR (string)
spec URN of the registered MISB Local Set used to decode this packet (e.g. "urn:misb:KLV:bin:0601.19")
.TP
\fBpacketIndex\fR (integer)
0\-based index of this packet within the decoded run
.TP
\fBlsVersion\fR (integer)
MISB ST 0601 Local Set version reported by tag 65, or 0 if absent
.TP
\fBvalueLength\fR (integer; bytes)
BER\-encoded value length of the outer Local Set
.TP
\fBchecksum\fR (object)
{expected, computed, valid}; tag 1 must match the engine's recomputation
.TP
\fBitems\fR (array)
decoded tags: {tag, name, value, units, raw?}; units is always present (empty string for tags without a unit)
.TP
\fBitems[].value\fR (polymorphic)
type follows the spec: int/uint/float/string/bool/enum/time. ST 0601 "error indicator" sentinels marshal to JSON null.
.TP
\fBitems[].raw\fR (string)
present only with \-\-raw; base64\-encoded value bytes
.TP
\fBdiagnostics\fR (array)
structural and per\-tag findings: {severity, code, message, tag?, tagName?, actual?, expected?, raw?}
.SS Time semantics
ST 0601 tag 2 (Precision Time Stamp) decodes to a TimeValue and serializes as RFC 3339 with microsecond precision in UTC, e.g. "2024\-01\-15T14:23:45.123456Z". When correlating frames against a wall\-clock event, prefer tag 2 over MPEG\-TS PES PTS — PTS is transport\-relative and resets on stream restarts.
.SS Schema stability
Schema is stable within klvtool 1.x: new fields are additive; existing field names and types do not change in minor releases. Diagnostic codes may be added but existing codes will not be repurposed.
.SS Common MISB ST 0601 tags
.TP
\fBTag 1 \(em Checksum\fR
16\-bit BCC over the packet; klvtool recomputes and reports valid/mismatch/malformed/N/A
.TP
\fBTag 2 \(em Precision Time Stamp\fR
wall\-clock at sample time (UTC); preferred timestamp for cross\-correlation
.TP
\fBTag 5 \(em Platform Heading Angle\fR (degrees)
0 = north, clockwise
.TP
\fBTag 6 \(em Platform Pitch Angle\fR (degrees)
.TP
\fBTag 7 \(em Platform Roll Angle\fR (degrees)
.TP
\fBTag 13 \(em Sensor Latitude\fR (degrees)
WGS\-84
.TP
\fBTag 14 \(em Sensor Longitude\fR (degrees)
WGS\-84
.TP
\fBTag 15 \(em Sensor True Altitude\fR (meters)
.TP
\fBTag 23 \(em Frame Center Latitude\fR (degrees)
WGS\-84; the geo\-anchor most GIS workflows want
.TP
\fBTag 24 \(em Frame Center Longitude\fR (degrees)
WGS\-84; pair with tag 23
.TP
\fBTag 25 \(em Frame Center Elevation\fR (meters)
.TP
\fBTag 65 \(em UAS LDS Version Number\fR
spec revision the producer claims to comply with
.TP
\fBTag 94 \(em MISB Tag (deprecated key list)\fR
rarely emitted by modern producers; surfaced for completeness
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Decode every metadata record as NDJSON for downstream pipelines
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool decode --input mission.ts --format ndjson --out frames.ndjson
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decode just one PID after `klvtool inspect` identifies it
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool decode --input mission.ts --pid 257 --format text
.fi
.RE
.PP
Step through packets with diagnostics highlighted
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool decode --input mission.ts --pid 257 --step
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
success — decoded zero or more packets without errors
.TP
\fB1\fR
decode failure (TS read error, ffmpeg failure, output write failure, or \-\-strict and any error\-severity diagnostic fired)
.TP
\fB2\fR
invalid usage (missing or malformed flags, unknown schema URN, \-\-step requested without an interactive terminal)
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable ANSI color in pretty output, regardless of TTY detection
.SH "REQUIRED TOOLS"
ffmpeg, ffprobe
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBklvtool\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-inspect\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-extract\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-diagnose\fR(1)
.SH "EXTERNAL REFERENCES"
.TP
